94: ## 3. Simulation Subsystem Specifications
95: 
96: ### 3.1 Mock HTMLMediaElement (`<video id="main-video-player">`)
97: Standard JSDOM leaves `HTMLMediaElement.prototype.play` and `pause` unimplemented (emitting `Not implemented: HTMLMediaElement's play() method` warnings). The M5 harness installs a high-fidelity media simulation onto `window.HTMLMediaElement.prototype` and `<video>` elements.
98: 
99: #### Media Element State & Properties:
100: - `currentTime`: Number (default `0`), with getter/setter. Setter triggers `seeking` and `seeked` DOM events.
101: - `duration`: Number (default `7200` seconds / 2 hours), configurable via `_setDuration(d)`.
102: - `paused`: Boolean (default `true`).
103: - `ended`: Boolean (default `false`).
104: - `seeking`: Boolean (default `false`).
105: - `readyState`: Number (default `0 = HAVE_NOTHING`; transitions through `1 = HAVE_METADATA`, `2 = HAVE_CURRENT_DATA`, `4 = HAVE_ENOUGH_DATA`).
106: - `buffered`: Mock `TimeRanges` object with `length`, `start(index)`, and `end(index)`.
107: - `playbackRate`: Number (default `1.0`).
108: - `volume`: Number (default `1.0`).
109: - `muted`: Boolean (default `false`).
110: - `textTracks`: Mock `TextTrackList` array with `mode` property (`'showing'`, `'hidden'`, `'disabled'`).
111: - `error`: Null or `MediaError` object `{ code: 4, message: 'MEDIA_ELEMENT_ERROR' }`.
112: - `src`: String getter/setter.
113: 
114: #### Media Element Methods:
115: - `play()`: Returns `Promise.resolve()`, sets `paused = false`, updates `readyState = 4`, dispatches `play` and `playing` events.
116: - `pause()`: Sets `paused = true`, dispatches `pause` event.
117: - `load()`: Resets `ended = false`, `currentTime = 0`, dispatches `loadstart` event.
118: - `canPlayType(type)`: Returns `'probably'` for `'application/x-mpegURL'`, `'video/mp4'`, and `'application/vnd.apple.mpegurl'`.
119: - `addTextTrack(kind, label, language)`: Creates and appends a mock `TextTrack`.
120: 
121: #### Simulation Control Hooks:
122: - `video._simulateTimeUpdate(time)`: Mutates `currentTime` and dispatches `timeupdate`.
123: - `video._simulateProgress(bufferedEndSeconds)`: Updates `buffered` ranges and dispatches `progress`.
124: - `video._simulateWaiting()`: Sets `readyState = 2` and dispatches `waiting`.
125: - `video._simulateCanPlay()`: Sets `readyState = 4` and dispatches `canplay`.
126: - `video._simulateEnded()`: Sets `currentTime = duration`, `ended = true`, `paused = true`, and dispatches `ended`.
127: - `video._simulateError(code, message)`: Sets `error = { code, message }` and dispatches `error`.
