160: ### 5.2 Local Proxy Requirement & Design
161: Because Chromium in webOS blocks client-side scripts from overriding the `Origin` header on media fetches and `<video>` tags, direct requests to `lightspeed.st` fail with HTTP 404.
162: 
163: **Solution**:
164: A lightweight local Node.js proxy service running at `http://127.0.0.1:3000` (or `8088`) packaged with the application.
165: - Exposes:
166:   - `/api/stream?tmdbId={id}&type={movie|tv}&season={s}&episode={e}&server={server}`: Executes the `crush.wasm` handshake, resolves the master playlist URL, rewrites playlist URIs to point through the local proxy, and returns the stream descriptor.
167:   - `/hls/proxy?url={encodedUrl}`: Forwards manifest and `.png` segment requests to `lightspeed.st`, injecting `Origin: https://cinejoy.pk` and `Referer: https://cinejoy.pk/`, streaming chunks back to `hls.js` with `Access-Control-Allow-Origin: *`.
168:   - `/api/servers`: Returns available streaming nodes.
169:   - `/health`: Liveness probe.
